"""
merge_pilot_research.py

Merges the results of the Thailand+India pilot research pass (68 hostels,
run via 14 parallel Agent subagents doing real WebSearch/WebFetch) into
hostels.json, and prints reliability stats (populated vs null per field)
for the cost/reliability estimate.

New fields added:
- services.bed_bug_reports: true|false|null  (true = credible recent report found)
- services.lockers: {"available": bool|null, "type": str|null, "note": str|null}
- services.hair_dryer_available: bool|null
- services.clothes_drying_facility: bool|null
- services.curfew_policy: str|null
- research_sources.pilot_2026_08: list of URLs used (per hostel, for audit)
- location.nearby (only for the 15 hostels that had none): same structured
  shape as normalize_nearby_and_boutique.py output, this time from genuine
  new research rather than re-reading existing text.

Not written to flagged_issues — that field already holds narrative
issue write-ups from the original research pass; these are new structured
fields alongside it, not a replacement.
"""
